{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Far be it from your servants.</b> חֻלִּין הוּא לָנוּ — a term of disgrace. And the Targum renders חַס לְעַבְדָּיךְ — 'spared be your servants' — meaning: spared by the Holy One, blessed be He, be it upon us to do this thing. And there are many instances in the Talmud of 'חַס וְשָׁלוֹם.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:26.121318165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}